    {
      "id": "d9527a20-4e5e-4da2-ba02-c795d966d04e",
      "phaseId": "f9a8c93b-6938-4644-88e4-f1d2d2f59d6d",
      "number": 350,
      "shortId": "NLSDL",
      "priority": 10,
      "shortName": "a-proportional-share-must-not",
      "title": "A proportional share must not be written as a fixed measure",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "# The problem\n\nTo make two containers take half a region each, `with_share` (`heca/src/chrome/mod.rs`) writes:\n\n```rust\nlayout.flex_grow = grow;\nlayout.height = heca_grid_ui::Length::Px(0.0);      // ← a FIXED measure\nlayout.min_height = Some(heca_grid_ui::Length::Px(0.0));\nlayout.flex_shrink = Some(1.0);\n```\n\n**A proportional share is being expressed by writing a fixed number**, which is what the user does not\nwant anyone doing (2026-07-28: *\"I don't want other developers to write fixed measure\"*). Worse, it is\nthree coupled fields whose combination is folklore: get one wrong and the split silently reverts to\ncontent-sizing, which is exactly the bug it was written to fix.\n\n# Why it is there\n\n`flex_grow` distributes only **positive free space**. Container content is routinely taller than a\nsidebar, so there is no positive free space to distribute — measured 2026-07-28: two containers took\n**1214px each inside a 600px body** and divided nothing. In CSS the answer is `flex: 1 1 0`; the base\nsize of 0 is what makes the whole region free space. With it: **296px each**, measured.\n\n**`Layout` has no `flex_basis`** (confirmed — `grep flex_basis heca-grid-ui/src/style.rs` is empty),\nso `height = Px(0)` is standing in for it. taffy *does* have `flex_basis` in its `Style`, so the\nconcept is available one layer down and simply was never surfaced.\n\n# What to build\n\n1. **Add `flex_basis: Option<Length>` to `Layout`** and map it in `to_taffy`\n   (`heca-grid-ui/src/style.rs`). That is the missing word in the vocabulary; everything below already\n   understands it.\n2. **Give the library one way to say \"take a share\"** so no caller assembles the trio by hand — a\n   builder on `LayoutExt` (`heca-grid-ui/src/builders.rs`), e.g. `share(n)`, meaning *n shares of the\n   parent's main axis*, setting grow + basis 0 + min 0 + shrink internally. Then:\n   - `with_share` becomes one call and stops naming a measure;\n   - the SDK's `Style` trait (`heca-view/src/build.rs`) exposes the same thing, so a **described** tree\n     can say it too — today it can only set `flex_grow`, which has the same trap;\n   - `grow()` stays as the raw flex knob for callers who genuinely want content-based basis.\n   Decide whether `grow()` should be *renamed* or documented as the low-level one, so the obvious name\n   is the one that behaves as expected.\n3. **Main-axis, not height.** `flex_basis` is main-axis relative like `flex_grow`, so one setter covers\n   a column and a row (the same reason `ContainerContribution::grow` is not called `height_grow`). Do\n   not add a per-axis variant.\n4. **Sweep for the same folklore elsewhere.** `ScrollRegion::new()` already sets `min_height: 0` and\n   `flex_shrink: 1` by hand with a long comment explaining why (`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/scroll_region.rs:274`).\n   Check whether that is the same idea written a second way, and whether it should go through the new\n   setter.\n5. **Tests must measure, not inspect flags.** A test asserting `flex_grow == 1.0` passed while the\n   layout was visibly broken (2026-07-28) — the measured-height test is what caught it. Assert\n   pixels: two shares of a 600px region are ~296 each, with content far taller than either.\n\n# Acceptance\n\n- No caller writes a fixed measure to express a proportion — not in `heca`, not in the SDK, not in a\n  described tree.\n- One setter, documented, with the trio behind it.\n- `docs/widgets.md` says how to take a share, next to R8 (the stretch contract) in\n  `docs/chrome-and-ui.md` — the two rules are read together.\n- Whole workspace green, clippy 0 warnings.",
      "notes": "",
